Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-25
Subject: Depack aasmcpu's in-memory tinsentry and TInsProp backend tables
License: expat

`compiler/x86/aasmcpu.pas` stores instruction metadata in two packed
records:

  TInsProp  with an indexed change array
  tinsentry with an indexed longint operand-type array

Those tables are only consulted in memory. Keeping them packed forces
aggregate indexed access through packed subobjects, which tp2cc rejects
and which would otherwise become misaligned aggregate access in the
translated bootstrap. Depack these two backend-table records; this does
not change any on-disk format.

--- a/compiler/x86/aasmcpu.pas
+++ b/compiler/x86/aasmcpu.pas
@@ -160,7 +160,11 @@ interface
         Ch_MRAX, Ch_MRCX, Ch_MRDX, Ch_MRBX, Ch_MRSP, Ch_MRBP, Ch_MRSI, Ch_MRDI
       );
 
-      TInsProp = packed record
+      { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc C++ bootstrap. This is
+        optimizer metadata, not an on-disk format, and its change-array is
+        only consulted in memory. Keeping it packed forces aggregate indexed
+        access through a packed subobject for no file-format benefit. }
+      TInsProp = record
         Ch : Array[1..MaxInsChanges] of TInsChange;
       end;
 
@@ -175,7 +179,13 @@ interface
     type
       TOperandOrder = (op_intel,op_att);
 
-      tinsentry=packed record
+      { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc C++ bootstrap. This
+        instruction-table entry is in-memory-only, and packing it misaligns
+        the `longint` operand-type array. tp2cc lowers that array to a C++
+        aggregate carrier whose indexed element access binds references to
+        the underlying elements; keeping this record packed therefore turns
+        normal operand-table lookups into misaligned-reference UB. }
+      tinsentry=record
         opcode  : tasmop;
         ops     : byte;
         optypes : array[0..2] of longint;
